# Run with: kanso play keyed_read_of_every_field_is_a_runtime_error.kso
# (and with --interp; both engines agree).
#
# Should: be refused by `kanso check`, the way chapter 03 says the keyed
# form is refused when it names every field ("a keyed read must omit at
# least one field"), or else just run and print "1 2".
# Does: running it stops with
# `error[runtime]: a keyed read omits at least one field; reading every
# field is the positional form`. A canonical-form rule arrives as a
# runtime failure. In the port's module (ugit/date.kso had
# `{ day month year } = civil days`) `kanso check` answered ok, and only
# `kanso test` found it. (`kanso check` on this one-file play program
# stops earlier, at the library-versus-statements rule.)
type pair
  left
  right

fn both p
  { left right } = p
  "{left} {right}"

print (both (pair 1 2))
